.\" Man page for fcitx5-nextless
.TH nextless 1 "2026-10-05" "0.2.0" "fcitx5-nextless"
.SH NAME
fcitx5\-nextless \- push-to-talk voice input addon for fcitx5
.SH SYNOPSIS
fcitx5 addon, loaded automatically. No standalone binary.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfcitx5\-nextless\fP is a push-to-talk voice input addon for the fcitx5
input method framework. It captures audio via PulseAudio, performs
speech recognition through configurable ASR backends, and commits the
recognized text to the active application.

Hold the \fBtrigger key\fP (default \fBRight Ctrl\fP, fully configurable in the
fcitx5 add-on settings) to start recording, release to stop and transcribe.
The recognized text is committed at the cursor position.
.PP
The input panel shows \fBlistening\fP, \fBprocessing audio\fP, and
\fBrecognizing\fP status. Network, service, timeout, microphone, and
no-speech failures are shown in that panel and are never inserted into the
application document.
.SH USAGE
.TP
\fBTrigger key\fP (long-press, default 300ms)
Start voice recording. Release to stop and transcribe. A short tap is ignored,
so the key keeps working as a normal modifier while you type.
.PP
Recording can start while an earlier cloud request is still recognizing.
Nextless preserves recording and commit order and targets the input context that
was active at the start of each recording. At most three recognitions,
including the active one, are queued. A newer recording is discarded with an
input-panel error when that limit is reached.
.TP
\fBShift+trigger\fP (or \fBCtrl+CapsLock\fP when the trigger is CapsLock)
Enter provider/denoiser switching mode. While holding the trigger key:
.br
\fB\(<- / h\fP  \-\- previous ASR provider
.br
\fB\(-> / l\fP  \-\- next ASR provider
.br
\fB\(ua / k\fP   \-\- previous denoiser
.br
\fB\(da / j\fP   \-\- next denoiser
.SH INSTALLING
Build from source (\fBmeson setup build --prefix=/usr\fP, \fBninja\fP,
\fBsudo meson install\fP), or package it: the repository ships a \fBPKGBUILD\fP
(Arch, \fBmakepkg -si\fP) and \fBdebian/\fP sources (Debian/Ubuntu,
\fBdpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b\fP, then \fBdpkg -i\fP the resulting
\fBfcitx5-nextless_*.deb\fP). ASR models are never part of the package
payload; run \fBnextless-get-models\fP after installing. Restart fcitx5
(\fBfcitx5 -r -d\fP) to load the add-on.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The full settings panel lives in the fcitx5 add-on configuration (Configure
Nextless under Add-ons): trigger key, default backend, timing, denoiser, model
dirs, threads, punctuation and cloud API keys. Saving writes the JSON files in
\fB~/.config/nextless/\fP in place (unknown keys are preserved) and applies to
the running engine immediately; the files remain the source of truth and can
still be edited by hand.
.SS Add-on settings (trigger key, default backend)
.TP
\fB~/.config/fcitx5/conf/nextless.conf\fP
Written by the fcitx5 "Add-ons / 输入法插件" configuration GUI, or edited by
hand. \fBHotkey\fP accepts any key, including bare modifiers such as
\fBControl_R\fP, \fBAlt_R\fP, \fBShift_L\fP, \fBSuper_L\fP and modifier
combinations; CapsLock is also supported and is then un-pressed for you so the
lock state never changes.
.RS
.nf
[Hotkey]
0=Control_R

DefaultProvider=zipformer
.fi
.RE
.SS User-facing (must edit)
.TP
\fB~/.config/nextless/\fP
Per-user configuration directory (doubao/qwen credentials, tuning).
.TP
\fBdoubao.json\fP
API credentials for ByteDance Volcengine ASR.
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "xxx", "resource_id": "volc.seedasr.auc"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBqwen.json\fP
API key for Alibaba DashScope Qwen3-ASR-Flash.
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "sk-xxx"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBnextless.json\fP
Interaction parameters.
.RS
.nf
{"activation_msec": 300, "notification_timeout": 2000, "debounce_count": 2}
.fi
.RE
.SS Advanced (optional, all have hardcoded defaults)
.TP
\fBadvanced.json\fP
All tuning parameters in one file. Sections:
.IR audio ,
.IR doubao ,
.IR qwen ,
.IR zipformer ,
.IR fire_red ,
.IR punctuation .
See default values in the distributed example.
.PP
For Doubao, \fBpoll_interval_msec\fP is the normal result polling interval.
The first query is sent after 300ms to improve short-utterance latency; later
queries use the configured interval.
.TP
\fBhotwords.json\fP (optional)
Mishearing correction table, \fB{"what it heard": "what you meant"}\fP.
Applied literally to the final text of every backend, before punctuation.
See ASR PROVIDERS below.
.SS Audio
.TP
\fBaudio.json\fP
Denoiser selection.
.RS
.nf
{"denoise": "speexdsp"}   \fR# none | speexdsp | deepfilter\fP
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBdeepfilter\fP (optional)
Runs the \fBdeep-filter\fP CLI from DeepFilterNet as an external process. It is
looked up in \fB~/.local/share/nextless/bin/deep-filter\fP, or wherever the
environment variable \fBNEXTLESS_DEEP_FILTER\fP points. Audio is resampled to
48 kHz for the model and back to 16 kHz for the recogniser.
Spawning, runtime and result are all bounded: if the binary is missing, fails,
exceeds 5 seconds (it is then killed) or returns the audio unchanged, that
utterance falls back to speexdsp, and three consecutive failures switch
deepfilter off until fcitx5 restarts.
.SH ASR PROVIDERS
.TP
\fBMock\fP
Returns "hello world" immediately. For testing without network.
.TP
\fBZipformer\fP (sherpa-onnx)
Local offline streaming model (~360 MB). Requires \fBsherpa-onnx\fP binary, both installed by \fBnextless-get-models\fP.
.TP
\fBFireRed\fP (sherpa-onnx-offline)
Local offline AED model (~1.2 GB unpacked). Requires \fBsherpa-onnx-offline\fP binary, both installed by \fBnextless-get-models\fP.
.TP
\fBDoubao\fP (ByteDance Volcengine)
Cloud API. Requires \fBdoubao.json\fP with API key and resource ID.
.TP
\fBQwen\fP (Alibaba DashScope)
Cloud API. Requires \fBqwen.json\fP with API key.
.TP
\fBHotwords\fP (post-processing, every backend)
The final text of any backend is first passed through the replacement table
in \fBhotwords.json\fP (e.g. \fB{"LIBR": "礼拜二"}\fP): longest key wins at each
position, replacements are never re-matched, and a missing, empty or
malformed file rewrites nothing. The packaged template only contains
\fBYOUR_\fP placeholder keys, which are dropped when parsing, so first-run
copies cannot alter real speech. Editing the file takes effect on the next
utterance.
.TP
\fBPunctuation\fP (optional post-processing)
Local backend results can be run through \fBsherpa-onnx-offline-punctuation\fP
(ct-transformer) to add ，。？. The ~62 MB model is opt-in
(\fBnextless-get-models --punctuation\fP) and applied on the recognition
thread (~0.2 s per utterance). If the model is missing or the run fails,
the raw text is committed; cloud backends are never touched.
Disable with the \fBpunctuation.enabled\fP key in \fBadvanced.json\fP.
.SH AUDIO PIPELINE
Recorded audio goes through:
.RS
.nf
PulseAudio capture
  \(-> ebur128 loudness normalization (-16 LUFS)
  \(-> denoising (speexdsp, or deepfilter when installed)
  \(-> VAD-based silence trimming
  \(-> WAV output
  \(-> ASR recognition
.fi
.RE
.PP
PulseAudio capture is asynchronous. On trigger release, Nextless returns
control to fcitx5 immediately, retains a short audio tail, then starts
processing and recognition.
.SH RELIABILITY
Doubao and Qwen use persistent serialized workers, allowing curl connections
to be reused while preserving result order. Zipformer and FireRed intentionally
run one local process per utterance.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fcitx5/conf/nextless.conf
Trigger key and default ASR backend (fcitx5 add-on settings).
.TP
.I ~/.config/nextless/
Configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nextless/
Local ASR models and sherpa-onnx binaries; installed by
.B nextless-get-models
(see README, "Get models (local backends)").
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nextless/sounds/
Optional replacements for the notification sounds (activate, deactivate, switch).
.TP
.I /usr/share/nextless/sounds/
Bundled notification sounds, played through paplay or pw-play.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/*/fcitx5/nextless.so
Addon shared library (multiarch path; on Debian/Ubuntu it is under x86_64-linux-gnu).
.TP
.I /usr/share/fcitx5/addon/nextless.conf
Addon manifest.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/RevolutionLA/nextless/issues\fP.
.SH AUTHORS
Nextless is a fork of \fBvinput\fP by xander-lin (MIT), maintained by RevolutionLA
with a configurable trigger key and offline-first defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fcitx5 (1)
